  "rationale": "The subject `requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.read_source.fn` has one obligation: criterion code reads sources through `ValidationContext.read_source`. That is a pointer to the operation's API. The operation's behavior belongs to `ValidationContext.read_source`, which the subject only cites. It needs no separate assessment here.\n\nThe marked test is `direct_source_reads_preserve_mapping_errors_and_record_only_successful_returns` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs`. It calls `ValidationContext::read_source` with an `OutlineData` item, which is the entry point the requirement names. It asserts these outcomes:\n- Unsupported items return an error and leave `dependencies()` empty.\n- A failing read returns an error and records nothing.\n- A successful read returns the content and records a `Dependency::Node` with the content's fingerprint.\n- The record from `finish` is current until the underlying text changes.\n\nThe same test module has a `ReadSource` criterion whose `execute` calls `cx.read_source(...)`. `deterministic_source_reads_reuse_saved_results` runs that criterion through `validation::refresh_evidence`. So criterion code using the method is exercised too. I did not read `ReadSource`'s `execute` body or that test's assertions, so this is based on the search snippets, which show only the call and the `refresh_evidence` runs. It adds support but is not needed for the judgment. The implementation sites are `procedure.rs#impl[ValidationContext<'_,%20D>]/fn[read_source]` and `sources.rs#impl[SourceAnalysis<P>]/fn[parse]`. I found no untested obligation or conditional behavior that the tests would miss.",
